# EigenScript gap: no inf/nan. Division by zero raises. EigenScript clamps
# every finite value in (1e308, DBL_MAX] to 1e308 (and the negative interval
# to -1e308), including literals (EigenScript#1286, "One overloaded number type").
# Lua:      print(1/0, -1/0, 1e308 * 10, 0/0 ~= 0/0) -> inf  -inf  inf  true
#           math.huge -> inf
# Expected: IEEE inf/-inf/nan values (Lua's float semantics), or a loud
#           refusal. EigenLua emits the direct operation (owner decision 2):
#           math.huge is 1e308 and x / 0 raises, as a Lua error.
# Actual 686d3b7d: 1e+308 for 1e308 * 10 (silent), and 1 / 0 raises
#           "division by zero".
# Rows: num_print (line 1) (D); events.lua (168) (S).
print of (1e308 * 10)
try:
    print of (1 / 0)
catch e:
    print of e.message
